```ts
ending: (body) => {
  if (body.includes("atomaton:ended=handoff")) return "handed-off";
  if (body.includes("atomaton:ended=done")) return "returned";
  return "";
},
```

That mirrors ENDED_TAG.read better (the real format). Then the notice body "A comment was removed. It said:\n\n<!-- atomaton:ended=done -->" → without quoted → "returned" event; with quoted → none. But the test doesn't assert the without-quoted behavior... it asserts events == ["asked"] only. For the test to be meaningful it should show the ending WOULD be read without quoted — otherwise it passes trivially. Let me add an assertion: the same notice without quoted → events ["asked", "returned"]. Let me update the stub and add that assertion.

